{"row_key": "S6_01_INVARIANTS:A4.2", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "inv:A4.2", "source_file": "fragments/part_A.tex, Statement A4.2", "source_line": 3440, "source_section": "The cotangent direct images and the decisive period scalar", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Correction", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Refuted: The claimed degree-one torsion along the cusp]\label{inv:A4.2}
The assertion in AC26 Remark 9.21, PDF page 81, that
$\Omega_{X/B}^1$ has torsion along $W\cup S_1\cup S_2$ is false.
Its torsion is supported precisely on $S_1\cup S_2$; its degree-one
cusp modules are torsion-free but not locally free on the double
locus.  The plural statement in Remark 1.3, PDF page 5, must be
qualified by degree: $\Omega^2_{X/B}$ does have torsion on the cusp
double locus.  The workbench's degree-one correction is correct;
it must not be extended to degree two.
