{"row_key": "WORKING_INV:thm:exact-bott-chern-aeppli", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "inv:C2.1", "source_file": "workbench/hodge_frolicher.tex", "source_line": 4257, "source_section": "Fr\"olicher, Bott--Chern, Aeppli, and Hermitian metrics", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Bott--Chern and Aeppli tables as functions of $h$]\label{inv:C2.1}\label{wb:thm:exact-bott-chern-aeppli}
With
\[
H^{p,q}_{BC}=
\frac{\ker\partial\cap\ker\bar\partial\subset A^{p,q}}
{\im\partial\bar\partial},\qquad
H^{p,q}_{A}=
\frac{\ker\partial\bar\partial\subset A^{p,q}}
{\im\partial+\im\bar\partial},
\]
the complete tables are
\begin{equation}\label{inv:eq:C-BC-A}
\begin{array}{c|rrrr}
q\backslash p&0&1&2&3\\\hline
3&0&0&1&1\\
2&0&h&2h&1\\
1&0&2&h&0\\
0&1&0&0&0
\end{array}_{BC}
\qquad
\begin{array}{c|rrrr}
q\backslash p&0&1&2&3\\\hline
3&0&0&0&1\\
2&0&h&2&0\\
1&1&2h&h&0\\
0&1&1&0&0.
\end{array}_{A}
\end{equation}
In particular, substitution of the value $h=1$ proved in \ref{inv:A3.1} gives
